  "articleBody": "Ever wonder how some tiny homes feel so open and inviting, while others feel, well, tiny? It often comes down to multifunctional living-space design. It’s not just about fitting things in; it’s about making spaces flexible and purposeful. Think about elements like furniture that transforms – a dining table that folds into the wall, a couch that becomes a guest bed, or even a kitchen island that doubles as a workspace. These features allow a single area to serve multiple purposes throughout the day, effectively expanding your usable square footage without adding an inch. Zen Tiny Homes specializes in these clever design strategies. We focus on creating efficient layouts and flexible living areas that adapt to your needs, whether you’re cooking, working, or entertaining. Our expertise isn't just about building small; it's about crafting homes that genuinely support your lifestyle, making 'less space' feel like 'more possibility.' From concept to construction, we work with you to ensure your home feels expansive, comfortable, and truly customized. If you’re dreaming of a tiny home that defies its dimensions, let’s chat about how thoughtful, multifunctional design can make that a reality.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-03"
}